+## Harness changes after the submitted run (as of 2026-09-06)
+
+These changes were made between 2026-08-27 and 2026-09-06 for evolution-arm pilots on
+Ouroboros 6.113.5 and are published as the operator patch
+`adapter_evolution_campaign.v61135.patch` (razzant/ouroboros,
+`devtools/benchmarks/continual_learning/operator_patches/`). None of them was active in the
+submitted run. They branch from PR #10 (`a691cf3`) and do not include the later upstream
+regeneration of `adapter_official_submission.v681.patch` (the `OUROBOROS_SUBAGENTS`
+transport from `run_clb.py` and the removal of the legacy HEAVY/CODE pins).
+
+### What ran, and on which engine
+
+The last end-to-end run of this adapter was on 2026-09-03: CL-Bench `run-all` groups
+`2026-09-03T05-22-33.505496Z` (control) and `2026-09-03T05-22-33.505495Z` (treatment),
+`sales_prediction`,
+`openrouter/anthropic/claude-sonnet-4.6`. The engine was Ouroboros 6.113.5 built from a
+local engine-fix branch, head `1ffa14d5`, 135 commits over the public
+razzant/ouroboros@`8d13373b` (VERSION 6.113.5) and not published. The runtime attestation
+recorded `clone_version=6.113.5` and `head=5fd3157e`, which is that head plus the
+harness-injected commit that seeds the `remote_work` skill. On the treatment arm the engine
+commits its own absorbed cycles into the read-write mount; that run ended at VERSION
+6.113.16. The runtime image `clbench-ouroboros:dev` was a pre-existing local build: the
+engine code is mounted from the clone and the image carries only dependencies. The upstream
+fix for stale delivery-control envelopes (`88948116`) is not in the evaluated engine's
+history.
+
+Active in that run: the restart gate in its earlier form (marker file plus health probe,
+900 s bound; it held 8 submits in the treatment arm), the single retry of a question
+cancelled by a restart, the 1800 s restart drain, the single-model reviewer slots with the
+scope scout, the sandbox lifetime override (the treatment arm ran 2 h 25 min and lost no
+container), and the turn-1 config attestation.
+
+Added after that run and exercised only by the unit tests above: the answer locator built
+on the official parser (2026-09-03, after the run finished); the evolution-boundary
+readiness wait with its shared budget, the current form of the restart gate, the promotion
+cadence `off` on the forced arm, the fail-closed forced request, and the handling of
+restart-shaped 503 refusals (2026-09-06).
+
+This adapter has not been run on any 7.x engine. Reading the code of razzant/ouroboros
+7.4.5 (`33da7a4f`, 2026-09-23) shows two breaks: the engine refuses native-seed trust to a
+skill manifest without `plugin_api: "2.0"`, so `remote_work` is not enabled and the live
+loop has no tools; and the task record no longer carries `cost_usd` or
+`cost_usd_with_children`, so the engine-task UsageEvents lose their cost. Independently of
+the engine version, a fresh image build is expected to fail: the engine's `requirements.txt`
+has been a pointer to `requirements-runtime.lock` since v6.97.0, on 6.113.5 as on 7.4.5, and
+the Dockerfile does not copy the lock. The 2026-09-03 run used a previously built image. The
+restart-refusal handling targets an admission fence that exists only in the local engine
+build and stays dormant on public engines.
+
+### Evolution arms and pilot shape
+
+Post-submission pilots run two arms per model that differ in exactly one system parameter:
+`evolution:false` (control) and `evolution:true` (treatment). Both carry
+`evolution_trigger:"forced"`, which is inert on the control arm (`on_instance_boundary`
+returns before any evolution work when evolution is off). Since 2026-09-06 the treatment
+arm sets `OUROBOROS_POST_TASK_EVOLUTION_CADENCE=off` while keeping
+`OUROBOROS_POST_TASK_EVOLUTION=true`, so a cycle starts only from the request the adapter
+files at a question boundary. The runs up to 2026-09-03 used the adapter's default cadence
+`every_n:1` (the engine's own default is `llm`), under which every finished task, including the auto-resume task the engine
+starts after a restart, files the next promotion, so cycle, restart, auto-resume and the
+next cycle can chain between two questions. The pilots are not the submitted recipe:
+`sales_prediction` only, `--runs 1`, `--task-parallelism 1 --per-task-parallelism 1`,
+stateless baseline skipped (`OUROBOROS_BENCH_SKIP_BASELINE=1`). The engine repository is
+mounted read-write on the treatment arm and read-only on the control arm.
+
+### Question boundary: the next question waits for the evolution round
+
+In PR #10 the boundary wait runs until the task timeout (900 s by default), and its early
+exit (request file gone and nothing running) does not tell a consumed request whose cycle
+is not yet enqueued from a finished cycle. The 2026-09-02 and 2026-09-03 pilots capped the
+wait at 300 s. Over the 12 completed cycles of the 2026-09-03 treatment run a cycle took
+464 s at the median and 920 s at most, and 14 of its 22 questions were submitted while an evolution task was running. That is the
+only way a benchmark task can be caught by the restart the cycle requests, because the
+engine enqueues an evolution task only when its queue is idle
+(`enqueue_evolution_task_if_needed` in `supervisor/evolution_lifecycle.py`).
+
+Now `on_instance_boundary` captures a baseline (server sha, campaign identity, both cycle
+counters) before publishing the forced request, publishes at most once per boundary, and
+then polls every 8 s until the engine is quiet by a host-visible predicate: no promotion
+request on disk and `evolution_mode_enabled` false; `/api/state` healthy with
+`evolution_enabled` false, zero pending and running tasks, empty `evolution_state` ids and
+no active direct-chat activity (the post-restart auto-resume task runs as one); no
+`pending_restart_verify` marker, claimed or not, and no unresolved restart obligation on
+the active transaction. Two consecutive quiet samples are required; any activity,
+unreadable state or sha change resets the count. If the `/api/state` payload does not carry
+the expected fields, the missing names are logged once and the boundary falls back to the
+previous counter-based early exits. The wait has one 1800 s monotonic budget per boundary;
+repeated cycles and restart retries inside it do not renew it, while a later wait that
+begins after the budget expired (a resubmit late in a long question, a format-repair
+submit) starts its own window. On the treatment arm the same predicate also runs before
+every question submit. On expiry the gate returns `reason="timeout"` with the blockers
+logged and the question is submitted anyway.
+
+### Engine restarts
+
+The engine's restart drain deadline is raised to 1800 s through
+`OUROBOROS_RESTART_DRAIN_MAX_SEC`; the engine default is 120 s, which the submitted run used.
+A question whose task record says it was cancelled by a restart is retried once. Before each
+submit `_await_pending_restart` waits out a pending restart: on the treatment arm through the
+readiness predicate above, elsewhere through the marker files and a health probe, inside the
+same budget. A restart-shaped HTTP 503 re-enters that wait without consuming a submit
+attempt. Restart-kill detection matches the word "restart" in the free-text task result,
+because the engine exposes no typed reason for it. Every boundary and pre-submit gate result
+(reason, cycle outcome, elapsed time, counters, blockers) is logged by the bridge.
+
+### Answer extraction
+
+The final action is located with the official adapters' candidate enumeration:
+`_json_candidates` and `_parse_action_text` are copied verbatim from
+`src/systems/claude/system.py` into `src/systems/ouroboros/action_parse.py` (the Codex
+adapter carries the same two functions), and a test pins the copies equal to the claude
+adapter. The live locator (`_final_answer_action`) walks `_json_candidates` from the most
+recent span and accepts the first that passes the shared `validate_with_coercion`. It
+re-implements the walk inline rather than calling `_parse_action_text`, and so differs from
+it in two ways: a candidate equal, ignoring `notes`, to the previously delivered payload is
+skipped while the current benchmark question has recorded no protocol step, and a walk that
+finds nothing returns None instead of raising the last validation error or retrying on
+`extract_json` of the whole text. `_parse_action_text` itself is used on the format-repair
+path and in the per-action loop. One property is inherited from the official parser: a
+fenced block is enumerated before the raw spans and duplicates keep their first position,
+so when the final answer is fenced and an earlier unfenced draft also validates, the draft
+wins the walk.
+
+The source text is up to the last 40 assistant outputs of the engine task, oldest to newest
+(`_task_assistant_text`; an unreadable observability directory degrades the source to the
+engine fields alone), followed by the engine's `result` and `final_answer`. If the walk finds
+nothing, two fallbacks follow: a schema-coercion model call over the final text
+(`_coerce_final`; cost recorded), which has no Claude Code analogue, and one in-container
+format-repair task (`_format_repair_action`; `OUROBOROS_FORMAT_REPAIR=0` disables), which
+mirrors the repair turn the Claude and Codex adapters run on a parse failure. Every pilot
+result produced so far, including the 2026-09-03 pair, used the previous locator (typed
+`final_answer`, then the last JSON span in the final text, strict schema validation).
+
+### Configuration deltas
+
+The pilot environment differs from the submitted block in `OUROBOROS_EFFORT_TASK=low`
+(submitted: `high`; the launcher applies one effort to all task types),
+`OUROBOROS_RESTART_DRAIN_MAX_SEC=1800`, `OUROBOROS_BENCH_SKIP_BASELINE=1`, and
+`CLBENCH_SHIM_BIND` unset on the pilot host (Docker Desktop, where the adapter default
+`127.0.0.1` is rewritten to `host.docker.internal` for the container). The remaining 17 of
+the 19 published keys are identical; the pilot scripts additionally export
+`OUROBOROS_BENCH_RUNS_ROOT`. Since 2026-08-30 `_overrides` also writes a same-model
+configured-subagent roster (`clbench-scope-scout`) into `OUROBOROS_SUBAGENTS` and pins
+`OUROBOROS_REVIEWER_SLOTS`: the triad as three `api_chat` rows on the solve model, scope and
+advisory through the scout. Without the pin the isolated settings inherit the host's
+structured reviewer slots, which then override the flat single-model review keys. A
+subagent route is therefore in use even though the solving agent still delegates nothing
+(depth 0 gates the `schedule_subagent` tool, and every route resolves to the same model).
+Turn-1 responses carry a `config_attestation` of the resolved host keys in
+`Response.metadata`.
